<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tabora</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tabora is a city in west-central Tanzania, in the land of the Nyamwezi. It grew from the 1840s around a settlement of Arab and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili merchants</a> in the chiefdom of Unyanyembe, becoming the chief inland depot of the caravan trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and slaves between the coast and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-tanganyika">Lake Tanganyika</a>. Explorers such as Burton, Speke, Livingstone and Stanley passed through, and under German rule it became an administrative centre and a station on the Central Railway.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tabora.jpg" alt="Tabora" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wesellgold entertainment · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Around_Kanyenye_Street_,Tabora_Manicipality,_Tanzania.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
